Here’s a typical "card grid" pattern using many `div` elements, with a container, an inner wrapper, and a `span` for the label. This setup is verbose (intentionally) to match your request.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Card Grid Pattern</title>
  <style>
    /* Outer grid container — the "row" */
    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 16px;
      padding: 16px;
      background: #f5f5f5;
    }

    /* Card container (outer card shell) */
    .card {
      background: #ffffff;
      border: 1px solid #ddd;
      border-radius: 8px;
      overflow: hidden; /* clean corners for inner elements */
      box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }

    .card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-4px);
    }

    /* Inner wrapper — holds content and label */
    .card-inner {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      padding: 16px;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    /* Label (span) inside inner wrapper */
    .card-label {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: #333;
      background: #f0f0f0;
      padding: 4px 8px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      align-self: flex-start; /* keep label tight to content */
    }

    /* Optional extra placeholder text inside inner wrapper */
    .card-title {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .card-description {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: #666;
      margin: 0;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

