### Structure breakdown (as requested):
- **`div.grid`** → the container (grid).  
- **`div.card`** → each card container (outer shell).  
- **`div.card-inner`** → inner wrapper (holds content).  
- **`span.card-label`** → the label (directly inside the inner wrapper).  
- Additional `div` elements (`.card-title`, `.card-description`) show typical content placement, but the core pattern is: `div.card > div.card-inner > span` (plus other divs for content).

This pattern is intentionally verbose — many nested `div`s — to match your "many divs" requirement. You can swap the grid to `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr))` for responsiveness if needed.

