    body {
      font-family: sans-serif;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 2rem;
      padding: 2rem;
      background: #f7f7f7;
    }

    .test-zone {
      background: white;
      border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
      width: 200px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    button {
      background: #4a90e2;
      color: white;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 4px;
      padding: 10px 18px;
      font-size: 16px;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: background 0.2s ease;
    }

    button:hover {
      background: #357abd;
    }

    .label {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: #555;
      font-size: 14px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- === Variant A: Top stacking (wrapper > inner > button) === -->
  <div class="test-zone" data-test-id="placement-top" data-variant="A">
    <div data-layer="tracking-group" data-event-context="top-placement">
      <div data-layer="button-wrapper" data-click-category="cta" data-click-label="top-CTA">
        <button type="button" data-analytics-id="btn-top">Placement A</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- === Variant B: Middle (extra nested for deeper tracking) === -->
  <div class="test-zone" data-test-id="placement-middle" data-variant="B">
    <div data-layer="outer-wrap" data-test-group="middle">
      <div data-layer="inner-wrap" data-placement="middle">
        <div data-layer="click-surface" data-custom-event="btn-middle">
          <button type="button" data-analytics-id="btn-middle">Placement B</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- === Variant C: Bottom / minimal nesting === -->
  <div class="test-zone" data-test-id="placement-bottom" data-variant="C">
    <div data-layer="section" data-analytics-context="bottom-area">
      <div data-layer="action" data-track="bottom-click">
        <button type="button" data-analytics-id="btn-bottom">Placement C</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How this supports A/B testing analytics:
- **Each variant has its own `data-test-id`** and `data-variant` attribute on the outer wrapper.
- **Multiple nested divs** per button, each with distinct `data-layer` names, so you can track at container, wrapper, or inner level.
- **The button itself includes `data-analytics-id`** for direct element targeting.
- You can easily add CSS selectors based on these attributes (e.g., `[data-variant="A"] button`) to attach event listeners or send custom events to your analytics tool.

To differentiate tracking events:  
- Use `data-variant` to segment the test arm.  
- Use `data-layer` to identify nesting hierarchy.  
- Use `data-event-context` or `data-category` for semantic meaning.

